  "reason": "No disclosed ordinary explanation for the FY22 PAT spike (2.1x vs FY20‑21 average) in the provided RHP pages. Financials (rhp:p45, p154) show revenue grew 46.5% but employee costs jumped 87% and other expenses 92%; the margin improvement stems largely from a large inventory build‑up (change in inventories ‑₹3.75cr vs ‑₹0.58cr) and lower finance costs, not from an order book, capex plan, or one‑off gain. The results discussion (rhp:p198) covers only 9M Dec‑22, not FY22 vs prior years. No narrative justification is present.",
